1
00:00:12,870 --> 00:00:14,620
Ah! Miss Stewart! Welcome!

2
00:00:14,620 --> 00:00:15,470
How are you?

3
00:00:15,470 --> 00:00:16,920
Fine, Somsak. And you?

4
00:00:16,920 --> 00:00:18,240
Fine, thank you.

5
00:00:18,240 --> 00:00:20,310
This is my friend Harry Bennett.

6
00:00:20,310 --> 00:00:21,190
Pleased to meet you.

7
00:00:21,190 --> 00:00:22,500
Very nice to meet you.

8
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:25,430
Any friend of Miss Stewart's is welcome at Somsak's.

9
00:00:25,430 --> 00:00:27,850
Follow me, please.

10
00:00:27,850 --> 00:00:28,820
I like it here.

11
00:00:28,820 --> 00:00:32,920
I do, too. I come here often.

12
00:00:32,920 --> 00:00:35,610
A special place for special people.

13
00:00:35,610 --> 00:00:39,360
Thank you, Somsak.

14
00:00:39,360 --> 00:00:45,700
Well! Nice restaurant.

15
00:00:45,700 --> 00:00:46,970
Would you like something to drink?

16
00:00:46,970 --> 00:00:49,660
Yes, I'd like a glass of ginger ale with ice.

17
00:00:49,660 --> 00:00:52,070
Harry, what would you like?

18
00:00:52,070 --> 00:00:53,950
Do you have a dry white wine?

19
00:00:53,950 --> 00:00:55,470
How about a California chablis?

20
00:00:55,470 --> 00:00:57,390
Chablis is fine.

21
00:00:57,390 --> 00:00:59,530
What would you like to eat?

22
00:00:59,530 --> 00:01:01,520
I'd like the mee krob.

23
00:01:01,520 --> 00:01:03,400
Harry, would you like to see a menu?

24
00:01:03,400 --> 00:01:04,350
No, it's Ok.

25
00:01:04,350 --> 00:01:09,890
I'll have the mee krob also.

26
00:01:09,890 --> 00:01:12,270
What is it?

27
00:01:12,270 --> 00:01:15,730
Crispy fried noodles. I love them.

28
00:01:15,730 --> 00:01:16,990
May I bring you a salad?

29
00:01:16,990 --> 00:01:18,130
Oh yes.

30
00:01:18,130 --> 00:01:19,580
What do you recommend today?

31
00:01:19,580 --> 00:01:21,640
I recommend rose-petal salad.

32
00:01:21,640 --> 00:01:24,580
Special for new friends.

33
00:01:24,580 --> 00:01:26,440
Rose-petal salad?

34
00:01:26,440 --> 00:01:28,140
Why not?

35
00:01:28,140 --> 00:01:33,310
I'll take care of everything.

36
00:01:33,310 --> 00:01:36,110
I hope you're hungry.

37
00:01:36,110 --> 00:01:43,680
What? Oh, yes. Starving. Well, I...

38
00:01:43,680 --> 00:01:47,640
Well, I ...

39
00:01:47,640 --> 00:01:50,030
What do you do at Universe Toy Company?

40
00:01:50,030 --> 00:01:52,960
I'm the vice-president of new toy development.

41
00:01:52,960 --> 00:01:54,870
Terrific!

42
00:01:54,870 --> 00:01:57,410
I know you 're a CPA.

43
00:01:57,410 --> 00:01:59,240
That's true. Harry Bennett,

44
00:01:59,240 --> 00:02:01,180
certified public accountant.

45
00:02:01,180 --> 00:02:02,910
I love numbers.

46
00:02:02,910 --> 00:02:03,970
I do some work for Smith and Dale,

47
00:02:03,970 --> 00:02:05,970
Your company's accounting firm.

48
00:02:05,970 --> 00:02:09,330
And so...

49
00:02:09,330 --> 00:02:10,870
Here we are.

50
00:02:10,870 --> 00:02:12,440
Yes.

51
00:02:12,440 --> 00:02:13,610
I have a daughter.

52
00:02:13,610 --> 00:02:15,920
I know. How old is she?

53
00:02:15,920 --> 00:02:17,370
She's nine years old.

54
00:02:17,370 --> 00:02:19,430
That's a nice age. What's her name?

55
00:02:19,430 --> 00:02:20,910
Michelle.

56
00:02:20,910 --> 00:02:33,350
Do you have a picture of her?

57
00:02:33,350 --> 00:02:35,720
She's very pretty.

58
00:02:35,720 --> 00:02:43,310
Thank you.

59
00:02:43,310 --> 00:02:45,980
Rose-petal salad.

60
00:02:45,980 --> 00:02:49,430
And there's a phone call for you, Mr. Bennett.

61
00:02:49,430 --> 00:02:52,240
Excuse me, Susan.

62
00:02:52,240 --> 00:02:54,780
I hope nothing is wrong.

63
00:02:54,780 --> 00:02:56,090
I'll get the rest of the dinner.

64
00:02:56,090 --> 00:03:10,260
Excuse me.

65
00:03:10,260 --> 00:03:12,190
Please forgive me, Susan, but...

66
00:03:12,190 --> 00:03:16,490
I have to leave. I feel terrible, but...

67
00:03:16,490 --> 00:03:18,220
What's the matter?

68
00:03:18,220 --> 00:03:20,080
My daughter isn't feeling well.

69
00:03:20,080 --> 00:03:22,590
Oh no! Is it serious?

70
00:03:22,590 --> 00:03:26,440
I don't know. The baby-sitter says she has a stomachache,

71
00:03:26,440 --> 00:03:27,290
and she's crying.

72
00:03:27,290 --> 00:03:29,010
I'll have to go home.

73
00:03:29,010 --> 00:03:29,940
Will you forgive me?

74
00:03:29,940 --> 00:03:32,980
Of course. I'm so sorry for Michelle.

75
00:03:32,980 --> 00:03:34,780
And you didn't have a chance to eat.

76
00:03:34,780 --> 00:03:36,240
Oh, it's OK.

77
00:03:36,240 --> 00:03:37,460
Let me take you home first.

78
00:03:37,460 --> 00:03:40,000
No, no. Please, go ahead.

79
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:42,010
It's our first date.

80
00:03:42,010 --> 00:03:43,550
We'll make another.

81
00:03:43,550 --> 00:03:46,470
Please don't worry.

82
00:03:46,470 --> 00:03:47,390
I'll phone you.

83
00:03:47,390 --> 00:03:51,360
I hope your daughter is all right. Good-bye.

84
00:03:51,360 --> 00:03:54,360
Good-bye.
